From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mauri de Souza Meneguzzo <mauri870@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 10:24:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: add HDMI 2.1 FRL support (trimmed for p03)

Add HDMI 2.1 Fixed Rate Link (FRL) on AMD display hardware: up to
48 Gbps across four lanes, so HDMI 2.1 sinks can run modes such as
4K@144 instead of being capped by HDMI 2.0 TMDS bandwidth.

Source: https://github.com/mauri870/linux-kernel/blob/7.2/0001-hdmi_frl.patch
(commit 8bd277c9f937).

Trimmed for p03, which already carries OGC's HDMI 2.1 VRR and ALLM work
(the ogc-* patches). The rule applied here is that this patch keeps only
the FRL link layer - the part OGC does not have - and everything that
OGC already implements is left to OGC. That means this patch MUST be
applied after the ogc-* patches; its context depends on them.

Dropped because OGC already provides it:

 - drm_crtc.c, drm_crtc.h, drm_mode_config.c, drm_mode_config.h,
   drm_atomic_uapi.c, ddc_service_types.h: dropped entirely.

 - struct drm_hdmi_vrr_cap, the vrr_cap/allm/fapa_start_location fields
   of struct drm_hdmi_info, and drm_parse_hdmi_gaming_info(): ogc-003
   adds byte-identical versions.

 - the passive_vrr_capable property, its attach/set helpers and its
   documentation: ogc-042 adds them.

 - the second VTEM path (build_vtem_infopacket_header(),
   mod_build_vtem_infopacket() and its own build_vtem_infopacket_data(),
   plus the PACKET_TYPE_VTEM case in mod_build_vrr_infopacket()).
   ogc-002 already emits VTEM through mod_build_infopacket_vtem(), which
   amdgpu_dm.c calls directly. Keeping both gave two static functions
   named build_vtem_infopacket_data() in one translation unit, and had
   OGC's VTEM overwrite this one on every commit. The MASK_VTEM_*
   register masks OGC's builder depends on are therefore kept as-is
   rather than replaced by this patch's VTEM_*_BIT set.

 - the whole ALLM layer: enum drm_allm_mode, the allm_capable and
   allm_mode connector properties with their attach/set helpers,
   drm_connector_state.allm_mode, amdgpu_dm_connector.hdmi_allm_capable,
   dc_stream_state.hdmi_allm_active and its stream update,
   update_allm_state_on_crtc_stream(), and the rewrite of
   mod_build_hf_vsif_infopacket() to read ALLM from the stream.
   ogc-005 implements HDMI 2.1 Section 7.6.6 instead: ALLM_Mode is set
   when Gaming-VRR is active and the sink advertises ALLM, passed
   explicitly to the existing four-argument mod_build_hf_vsif_infopacket().
   Nothing here forces ALLM on, and no new uAPI property is added.

 - the rename of enum adaptive_sync_type (FREESYNC_TYPE_PCON_* to
   ADAPTIVE_SYNC_TYPE_PCON_*). Cosmetic, and the original missed two
   call sites, leaving undefined identifiers. Only the genuinely new
   ADAPTIVE_SYNC_TYPE_HDMI = 5 is kept, with its case added to
   mod_build_adaptive_sync_infopacket().

 - amdgpu_dm.c: the two hunks rewriting the HDMI branch of
   amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(). That is VRR policy and OGC's
   version is kept. The helpers left unused by that (aconn_range_from_hdmi(),
   mccs_is_freesync_available()) and the locals that went with them
   (hdmi_vrr, check_mccs_freesync, pcon_allowed) are dropped too, and
   the as_type local the retained OGC code needs is restored.

 - amdgpu_dm_helpers.c: the original replaced
   dm_is_freesync_pcon_whitelist() with dm_helpers_is_vrr_pcon_compatible()
   and deleted dm_get_adaptive_sync_support_type(). Both are still used
   by code p03 keeps, so dm_helpers_is_vrr_pcon_compatible() is added
   alongside them and dm_get_adaptive_sync_support_type() keeps its
   prototype in dm_helpers.h.

The FRL data path is intact end to end: drm_hdmi_frl_cap defined in
drm_connector.h, filled by drm_parse_max_frl_rate() in drm_edid.c,
copied into dc_edid_caps by populate_hdmi_info_from_connector(), and
consumed by dc_stream.c which promotes the signal to
SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL when frl_caps.max_rate > 0. The new HPO HDMI
stream and link encoders live in dc/hpo/dcn30/ and are wired into
dc/hpo/Makefile.

Signed-off-by: Mauri de Souza Meneguzzo <mauri870@gmail.com>
